meta {
  name: find movie by id
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{tmdb_base_url}}/movie/:movie_id?language=en-US&append_to_response=credits,videos
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  language: en-US
  append_to_response: credits,videos
}

params:path {
  movie_id: 55
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{tmdb_api_key}}
  accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get Movie by ID
  
  Returns the primary information about a movie.
  
  `movie_id` **550** is Fight Club — a good default to sanity-check the response shape.
  
  ## Key response fields used by rate-it
  
  | Field | Maps to |
  |-------|---------|
  | `id` | `Media.ExternalID` |
  | `title` | `Media.Title` |
  | `poster_path` | `Media.PosterPath` |
  | `release_date` (year part) | `Media.ReleaseYear` |
  
  Source is always `tmdb`, type is `movie`.
  
  ## Auth
  
  Use a **Bearer token** (API Read Access Token from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api).
  Set `tmdb_api_key` as a secret variable in your environment.
}
